infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title forRoot vs forRootAsync: where do the options come from?
  compares
    - label forRoot
      children
        - label Options are a literal object
          desc Caller passes the StorageOptions value at the call site
        - label Bound via useValue
          desc The method wraps that literal object in a useValue provider
        - label Synchronous
          desc Resolved immediately, no DI lookup before the value exists
        - label Use for static constants
          desc A connection, client, or secret known up front
    - label forRootAsync
      children
        - label Options come from another provider
          desc Values live in ConfigService, not at the call site
        - label Bound via useFactory plus inject
          desc The factory runs after its inject dependencies are constructed
        - label Asynchronous and deferred
          desc Breaks the chicken-and-egg of needing config before the module
        - label Use for ConfigService and .env
          desc Per-environment, async, or secrets-manager values
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
